# Quill, ashore. One tree, a node per place.
dialogue quill3
  # The wreck and the lagoon shore: the boat banter.
  node boat quill "Boat's beached. And I'm not waiting with it, before you ask. Somebody has to stop you filling in forms at a man with a cutlass."
    > "You could wait with the boat. It's very safe." if not seen:quill3.safe -> safe
    > "Thank you for rowing." if not seen:quill3.rowing -> rowing
      add aff 1
    > "What did the captain say, exactly?" -> plan
    > "Shall we?" -> after
  node safe quill "So's a drawer. You tried that for three years. How was it?"
    > "What did the captain say, exactly?" -> plan
    > "Point taken." -> after
  node rowing quill "I didn't row for you. I rowed because you row like you're signing something in triplicate. …You're welcome."
    > "What did the captain say, exactly?" -> plan
    > "Shall we?" -> after
  node plan quill "Find anyone alive, run a new flag up the wreck's mast, and she brings the Marrow in through the Needle. If fifteen's still up when the fog lifts, we're dead and she's very sorry."
    > "She said “very sorry”?" -> sorry
    > "Then we'd better not be dead." -> after
  node sorry quill "She said “sorry”. I added the “very”. I'm navigator now; I'm allowed to round up."
  node after quill "After you, cargo. If anything bites, I want to see what."
  # Inside the wreck.
  node cabin quill "Your father keeps a tidy wreck. That's his desk. You're a clerk. Go on; I can see your fingers twitching from here."
    > "That's my mother, on the wall." if looked:arcadia_cabin.portrait and not seen:quill3.mother -> mother
      add aff 1
    > "It's not tidy. The whole room is at an angle." -> angle
    > "Give me a minute." -> minute
  node mother quill "I guessed. She's got your face, only she looks like she'd use it to win arguments. …I'll look at the wall for a bit. In case you want to tell her anything."
  node angle quill "Everything's at an angle on a ship, cargo. This one's just stopped pretending."
  node minute quill "Take two. The wreck's been waiting three years. It can wait for a clerk to breathe."
  node shaken quill "You all right?"
    > "No. But I think I'm going to be." if not seen:quill3.going -> going
      add aff 1
    > "I've been called an idiot in writing. By two people. In one morning." -> two
  node going quill "Good. That's the right order to say it in."
  node two quill "Three, counting me. I'm counting me."
  # At the gate.
  node gate quill "He's got a clipboard, cargo. This is your fight. I'll hold your coat."
    > "Is a navigator a ship's officer?" if seen:pike.need and not bill_signed -> officer
    > "You could just climb the fence." -> fence
    > "Wish me luck." -> luck
  node officer quill "It says so in the Marrow's log. In your handwriting. …Give me the bill, then, before I come to my senses."
  node fence quill "I could. Then he'd blow that whistle, and every Weather man on the key would come and be polite at me. I'd rather watch you do it properly."
  node luck quill "You don't need luck. You need a date, a stamp and a signature. Same as a wedding, Marta says."
  # Countersigning the bill (combos give it to her; rooms_act3.ts).
  node sign narrator "She reads every line of it, which nobody ever does, and signs at the bottom in careful capitals: QUILL, NAVIGATOR. Then she looks at it for a long time."
    -> signed
  node signed quill "First thing I've ever signed as anything. …It looks good. Don't say it looks good."
    > "It looks good." -> looks
      add aff 1
    > "It looks adequate." -> adequate
  node looks quill "I said don't. …Thank you. Take it before I underline it."
  node adequate quill "Adequate. I'll take it. That's a whole rank above what the lookout used to get."
  # The Weather Works.
  node works quill "Kelp smoke. Same as the crates on the Marrow. That big brazier's doing most of the work; put it out and the fog has nothing to stand on."
    > "And then?" -> then
    > "I'd need something wetter than paperwork." -> wetter
  node then quill "Then we run, cargo. I'm good at running. You'll be good at it by the end."
  node wetter quill "Everything's wetter than your paperwork. There's a whole lagoon out there. Find it a bucket."
  # Through the bars of the store hut.
  node hut quill "Don't look so pleased. You've finally got me in a box with a label on."
    > "I'm getting you out. I promise." if not seen:quill3.promise -> promise
      add aff 1
    > "You look very official behind bars." -> official
    > "Did he really call you cargo?" -> cargo
  node promise quill "I know. That's the annoying part. Go and be a clerk at him."
  node official quill "Say that again when I'm out, cargo. I dare you."
  node cargo quill "Unaccompanied cargo. Pending inspection. …I'm never calling you that again. That's a lie. But I'll feel bad about it."
  # Free, in the salt camp, with his father watching.
  node camp quill "Don't look at me like that. Your father's watching. …He's still watching. He's waving."
    > "He does that." -> waves
    > "Let him watch." if not seen:quill3.watch -> watch
      add aff 1
  node waves quill "Go and talk to him, cargo. You've waited three years. I've waited about a minute and I'm already sick of it."
  node watch quill "…All right. Let him. But I'm not waving back."
  # Back on the wreck with flag sixteen.
  node flag quill "Go on. Run it up. You've been carrying it like it's a baby."
    > "It's a very important baby." -> baby
  node baby quill "It's a flag made of your shirts, cargo. The halyard's on the mainmast. Up."
